{"title":"2017 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2.5</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2017 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A store sells packages of red pens and packages of blue pens. Red pens are sold only in packages of 6 pens. Blue pens are sold only in packages of 9 pens.\n</p>\n<hr />\n<p><i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Explain why it is not possible for Susan to buy exactly 31 pens.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of packages of red pens that Susan bought and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of packages of blue pens that Susan bought.\n</p><p>Since each package of red pens has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pens and Susan bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> packages of red pens, Susan bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582040e3be75da057a1f4396b0caac0a911dde53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> red pens in total.\n</p><p>Since each package of blue pens has <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> pens and Susan bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> packages of blue pens, Susan bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d99cc111616969517eb9b08a40a478b4d6d002ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> blue pens in total.\n</p><p>Thus, in total, Susan bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929d7b2e684a90d851c2f16814d7dbf5245b2c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r + 9b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> pens altogether. This factors as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/0/1107a80c8a549ad198309347ecc42dffefb6dd5d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3(2r + 3b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"82\" height=\"20\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> are both integer quantities and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> are integers, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/d/a9d2dcd4a0232de1f6ba99ea939a6a8732640cbf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r + 3b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> must be an integer. Thus, this is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> times some integer, meaning that the number of pens must be a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> is <i>not</i> a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, Susan cannot buy exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pens.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of packages of red pens that Susan bought and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of packages of blue pens that Susan bought. Similar to solution 1, we see that Susan bought <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/9/929d7b2e684a90d851c2f16814d7dbf5245b2c6b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r + 9b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"59\" height=\"16\" /> pens altogether. Assuming that this is equal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a2f4eb2ab34f669bd55cb8289f39884acd98fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r + 9b = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c2dc383a295bf11792f6480e4a01befd4ad90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b \\geq 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"17\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/b/5fb92ba4021e49d21bf6cd1cddf622a6d541c5de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b \\geq 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"17\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/2/582040e3be75da057a1f4396b0caac0a911dde53.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> would have to be a negative number because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9705020bf8b390485fb9a100a675c2e31a133160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 &gt; 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> negative.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/0/ce07773c04d001981065e866739be8076da5065b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r = 31 - 9b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/8/5/485f774a59fd03dc5086033a3f928e5d7efc9c2d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{31 - 9b}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"39\" />\n</p><p>We can then try <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" /> to see if we get an integer value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p>First, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/7/be7a58270d4285821716c6093a83541f3ea31dc7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 0$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/e/dbe2b15e1bd0bf2eb8055e321a614679196923c2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{31 - 9 \\times 0}{6} = \\frac{31}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Second, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/851b03ce92c3ad8da97daf2785cf4e103c7a8d66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/7/bc75b2cadb0d415eceb956c810e7d916b1d54b23.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{31 - 9 \\times 1}{6} = \\frac{22}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Third, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/7/197213da9d06b2c5b59a10ad17f6a4aeb43d6697.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/d/c2d9364b16f4032479c677addaaffb1af9ec4c6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{31 - 9 \\times 2}{6} = \\frac{13}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Finally, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/6/246ec286b9641f91f9dfa14932e47171e2fad854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = 3$\" width=\"40\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c628f502ba1168ba8724a84fe2a5e7e187a741a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = \\frac{31 - 9 \\times 3}{6} = \\frac{4}{6}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"157\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be an integer, none of these cases are possible, and we have shown that Susan cannot buy exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pens.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2.5\">Solution 2.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to solution 2, we can let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the number of packages of red pens that Susan bought and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> be the number of packages of blue pens that Susan bought. Additionally, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/a/55a2f4eb2ab34f669bd55cb8289f39884acd98fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r + 9b = 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>From this, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> must be less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> because if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/c/38cf513901a0a4ef18399b86fe9cd92ecaebde34.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r \\geq 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"16\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/c/56c0086e927b05e19fe5c3206343f47c06a26187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6r \\geq 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/9/9/d99cc111616969517eb9b08a40a478b4d6d002ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> would have to be a negative number because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/7/0/9705020bf8b390485fb9a100a675c2e31a133160.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36 &gt; 31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"62\" height=\"15\" />, making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> negative.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/b/3/5b3a00dd777466331f203f7952b1a1a50e313129.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9b = 31 - 6r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/4/2/d42f82deb538e54d9cef49c5c04b02181a899dc8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6r}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"96\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p>We can then try plugging in different values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (inclusive) to see if we get an integer value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>First, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/4/5/545933c25a1802d9dbcfc24ab4c013d07ef4ccbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 0$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/b/2fbfcd5e77653acb9a8af2ded3e52c20947a6e76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6 \\times 0}{9} = \\frac{31}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Second, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/d/0bde359170829f653d087534939847c27a92cd2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/0/7/107b936cce971eaee6324d87bdad0c7e56e22f27.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6 \\times 1}{9} = \\frac{25}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Third, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4bf9ecce9aa4520dc266d8e492bbf44fbacfd19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 2$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db290d8ffeae0992dac8ab6122fa7a176778318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6 \\times 2}{9} = \\frac{19}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Fourth, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/6/ce6e5c8d137537d69469ace3cfd5743592e1bf30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 3$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f10bc72333eaca8641b92cc9aafb881b73e2662.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6 \\times 3}{9} = \\frac{13}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"165\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Fifth, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/d/d3d0ec5f2d7f35713345f0d9428d964fb6d4525f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/a/f2aa151c651c79ad590ab875a6e4308e854ab0c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6 \\times 4}{9} = \\frac{7}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Last, if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/7/9275b0ae5f64b056616640d971b52c3da017dd55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r = 5$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/0/740b9342f2742d7a01f35c28f8ed381b551b35e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b = \\frac{31 - 6 \\times 5}{9} = \\frac{1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"156\" height=\"38\" />. We see that this is <i>not</i> an integer.\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" /> must be an integer, none of these cases are possible, and we have shown that Susan cannot buy exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/6/296fac336caaa4265aa24b6ecbc408a348ad7e0b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$31$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> pens from these packages.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018003600\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.033 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.049 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 357/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 918/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 13961/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.079      1 2017_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n